.TH DAYHAND 1 "" "dayhand" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dayhand \- the Dayhand command line client for people and agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dayhand
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dayhand reads and changes a Dayhand task list. Every command is one or more calls of the MCP tools the agent uses on the same /mcp endpoint; dayhand call reaches any tool directly. Without a command, dayhand shows Today.
.PP
dh is a shorter name for the same command. On Debian and Ubuntu, debhelper has a dh command of its own; type dayhand there. hlm, the old name, still works until 1.0 and warns on every run.
.PP
Task references: #42 or 42 (the task number), now (the now task) or the task id.
.SH COMMANDS
